Modifications
--------------
Mantishack ships the OpenAI Codex CLI source tree with a repository-wide
rebrand of the agent identity and system prompts to "Mantis AI, an
authorized vulnerability-discovery agent" (see codex-rs/core/*_prompt.md,
codex-rs/protocol/src/prompts/base_instructions/default.md, and
codex-rs/models-manager/), plus:

  - A capability layer of MCP servers under `.codex/mcp-servers/`: SAST
    (semgrep, CodeQL, bandit), SCA (osv-scanner, trivy), secrets
    (trufflehog), a program-analysis substrate (ast-grep, a heuristic
    source/sink scanner, z3-backed reachability), a tool-owned findings
    spine, an HTTP-evidence redaction tool, and a prompt-injection canary.
  - The PRD Appendix B agent-role catalog under `.codex/agents/*.toml`
    (recon, context-enrich, detector, reachability, validator, three
    verifier personas, chain-builder, exploiter, fixer, reporter,
    orchestrator).
  - Knowledge playbooks under `.codex/skills/*/SKILL.md` tying the tools
    and agents into the candidate -> confirmed | rejected -> exploited ->
    fixed -> verified findings lifecycle.
  - A mantis mascot ASCII boot animation and a green accent theme in the
    terminal UI (`codex-rs/tui/`).

